mment-42-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: that you must finally reach Athens; may you preserve this in all your fear. Not by the straight path, for from it the pursuers soon divert him, but by a thousand detours yet finally. ⟦2⟧. like ⟦3⟧ ⟦4⟧ (= ⟦5⟧)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-1-mentioned1", "translation": "remember"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-1-mentioned2", "translation": "let not fear seize you"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-1-mentioned3", "translation": "let not deceit overcome your mind"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-1-mentioned4", "translation": "let it prevail"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-2-comment1", "translation": "89 ⟦1⟧ like ⟦2⟧ (⟦3⟧. ⟦4⟧);"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-2-mentioned1", "translation": "kindred blood"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-2-mentioned2", "translation": "kindred"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧= ⟦2⟧, ⟦3⟧ since Homer (below 606. 608)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-3-mentioned1", "translation": "blood"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-3-mentioned2", "translation": "race"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-3-mentioned3", "translation": "kinship"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-4-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ stands parallel to the adjective. –"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-4-mentioned1", "translation": "of a common father"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-5-comment1", "translation": "90 ⟦1⟧ like ⟦2⟧ ⟦3⟧, ⟦4⟧ etc. ⟦5⟧, ⟦6⟧ is preferably the chthonic one (Preller-Robert 407, 1), yet nothing stood in the way of turning the word differently."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-5-mentioned1", "translation": "eponymous"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-5-mentioned2", "translation": "Hermes the guide"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-5-mentioned3", "translation": "escort"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-5-quote1", "translation": "of whom Zeus the averter of evil may be named for the city of the Cadmeans"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-42-6-comment1", "translation": "V. 90 ⟦1⟧ counterpart to ⟦2⟧ 78. Difficulties have been made by the ending, but Hermann, Dindorf, Weil simply follow the transmitted text and the scholiast's e